I. PREFACE: THE THERMAL IMPASSE
Traditional magnetic storage and spintronic interconnects, governed by Spin-Transfer Torque (STT) and electrical charge transport, have reached a physical limit. As data densities increase, the "Thermal Tax"—manifesting as Joule heating (Q = I squared times R times t) and electron-mediated decoherence—grows exponentially. This creates a fundamental bottleneck for petascale integration and long-term data integrity.
NEPTUNE-PHX, conceived by Juho Artturi Hemminki, is the definitive departure from charge-based magnetic switching. It is a resonant, phonon-driven orchestration layer that manages the magnetic state of matter via lattice-wave interference. NEPTUNE-PHX enables a seamless transition from discrete bit-flipping to a coherent wave-front manipulation, maintaining a zero-dissipation profile. It is the first protocol to treat magnetic data as a harmonic resonance field rather than a current-driven state.

II. THE DYNAMIC COHERENCE PROTOCOL
The NEPTUNE-PHX does not operate on brute-force magnetic fields; it adapts its operational mode based on the phonon-dispersion characteristics of the FCC Nickel (Ni) lattice (lattice constant a0 = 6.65 a.u.).
Phase 1: Localized-Harmonic Mode (wavevector q < 0.1)
At low wavevector densities, NEPTUNE-PHX functions as a high-precision point-to-point magnetic gate. The G-STORM core manages individual atomic spin alignment using a Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) that neutralizes thermal jitter in real-time.
Phase 2: Resonant-Field Mode (wavevector q = 0.5 to 1.0)
As the wavevector approaches the X-point (0, 0, 1), NEPTUNE-PHX shifts into a "Coherent-Resonance" state. It ceases to fight lattice vibrations and instead harvests them. Phonon energy is utilized as the primary carrier for angular momentum transfer, reinforcing the spin-flip torque while requiring zero electrical input.
Phase 3: Universal Spin-Continuum Mode (N -> infinity)
At the limit of massive array integration, NEPTUNE-PHX achieves mathematical saturation. The boundaries between individual magnetic domains vanish. Information is transmitted as a continuous Magnon-Phonon wave-front. In this state, the data becomes functionally indestructible; the loss of a billion atoms is mathematically irrelevant to the integrity of the coherent magnetic stream.

