The determinism of NEPTUNE-PHX is rooted in absolute quantum mechanical constants and the coupled Hamiltonian framework.
3.1 Phase-Harmonic (PH) Synchronization
Every spin-site (i) is locked into a specific phase offset governed by the Golden Ratio (phi = 1.618...). This prevents unwanted interference and destructive phonon-clashing.
Formula: Phase(i) = (i * phi) modulo 2*pi
This ensures the "beat" of the billion-spin array is distributed evenly across the temporal spectrum, eliminating ground bounce and EMI spikes.
3.2 X-Link Magnon-Phonon Coupling (chi)
The coupling between the lattice vibration (omega) and the spin-wave (Omega) is defined by the X-Link operator (chi), creating a holographic projection of data across the crystal.
Formula: chi(N) = Integral [ Hamiltonian_phonon(omega) tensor_product Hamiltonian_magnon(Omega) + g_interaction(a_daggerm + am_dagger) ] dn
As the wavevector (q) reaches the X-point, the switching reliability (R) asymptotically approaches absolute unity:
Formula: Limit (q -> 1) R_neptune = 1 - (1/N) to the power of phi
3.3 Phonon-Induced Effective Field (B_eff)
The lattice displacement field generates a virtual magnetic field for non-dissipative switching.
Formula: B_effective = - ( 1 / (mu_zero * Ms) ) * partial_derivative_of_Hamiltonian_interaction / partial_derivative_of_m
Component focus: B_effective_x(t) = ( (2 * B2) / Ms ) * strain_xz * sin(omega_q * t)
This field overcomes the magnetocrystalline anisotropy (Ku) using zero current (I = 0).
